data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":376,"item_id":"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb42172ad481919204b621e9689f3d","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy graph repair; prior-candidate.json graph/R001,R002,R003,R004 and source inventory\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"I read the supplied task inputs and core NL0 rules, inspected the recovered integration-by-parts theorem's exact probed signature and official source opening, and identified the required repair boundary. The existing graph requires further drafting: export complete time-window support/regularity facts from N001, revise R004 to use N001 and the recovered bilinear integration-by-parts theorem with its integrability/Frechet derivative hypotheses proved, repair empty support domination, define the Euclidean Borel/Lebesgue ambient and compact-measure fact with probed sources, and establish zero-integral in R001. No unsupported mathematical implication has been judged to be a substantive gap; this is ordinary unfinished source registration and graph drafting. I have not submitted an artifact or claimed a check/Audit A acceptance.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"The frozen task inputs and prior-candidate statements, Audit A findings, and recovered-library-source.json; checked M011 query evidence and Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/LineDeriv/IntegrationByParts.lean lines 1–100.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Read SKILL.md, nl0-stage.md, nl0-format.md, self-containment.md, nl0-authoring.md; read audit-findings.json, frozen-target.md, problem.md, source-context.md, recovered-library-source.json and prior-candidate.json. Verified M011 declaration signature, source hash, commit, theorem kind and axioms via probe_library; read official source documentation and hypotheses setup. Still need finish patch, probe/register compact measure facts and any other replacement source, structurally check, then submit the revised graph for fresh scoped Audit A.\\\"}\"}"}

